**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `constructor-unit-tests`: 

**How to implement.** Copy-in and location, the two kit verbs an attach needs, in both implementations (001 §E 'Attaching a file from outside the kit copies it into data/, keeping its name and suffixing on collision', 'Lab files are read-only for the app', 'Writes are atomic (write *.tmp, then replace)'; 001 §P '`KitProxy` … copy-in'; the S4.1 brief: copy a file in (S4.2)). (1) `KitProxy` (`KitFolders.fs`, steps 125-131) gains two fields, each with a one-line doc. `tryKitPathOf : FileName -> KitRelativePath option` answers the kit-relative path of an absolute file name that lies inside the kit, through `KitFolder.tryKitPathOf` (step 132), so both implementations share one rule. `copyInFile : KitDataFolder -> FileName -> FileByteContent -> Result<KitDataFile, KitError>` writes the bytes as a NEW file in the data folder. Its name is the leaf name given, or the one `copyTargetFor` (step 132) picks over every file and folder directly in that folder. It creates the folder and its parents when missing, and answers the file exactly as `readDataFile` (step 128) reads it back. It never replaces a file, because the app never writes a lab file (001 §E). (2) `InMemoryKitFolder` (step 125) gains `member this.kitFolder : KitFolder`, the folder it stands for, `KitFolder (FolderName "C:/in-memory-kit")`, against which its proxies locate names. It also gains `member this.removeLabFile (path : KitRelativePath) : Result<unit, KitError>`, an outside writer deleting a file: `MissingKitFileErr` when absent, and the `.kit-json` path refused with `InvalidKitPathErr`, as `placeLabFile` refuses it. `KitProxy.createInMemory`: `tryKitPathOf` is `folder.kitFolder.tryKitPathOf`. `copyInFile` decodes the bytes as UTF-8 with a leading byte-order mark dropped and stores the text at the chosen path in the folder's one map of texts, adding its parent folders, so `readDataFile` then answers it hashed as its UTF-8 bytes, as step 128's double does. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Storage/CatalogueFolderStore.fs`: the body of `FileName.writeBytesAtomically` (step 126) becomes one private body over `ExistingFilePolicy` (`Softellect.Sys.Primitives.ExistingFilePolicy`, STL `Sys/Primitives.fs`, reused). It writes `<file>.tmp`, then moves it onto the file, replacing it under `OverwriteExistingFile` (`File.Move(tmp, file, true)`) and never under `RefuseExistingFile` (`File.Move(tmp, file, false)`). On any failure it deletes the `.tmp` and answers `FileIoExn`. `writeBytesAtomically` calls it with `OverwriteExistingFile`, so step 126's facts stay green unchanged. New `member this.writeNewBytesAtomically (bytes : byte[]) : Result<unit, StorageError>` calls it with `RefuseExistingFile`. A declaration whose signature carries the bytes is marked as step 126's is. (4) `KitFolderStore.fs`, `KitProxy.create` (steps 126-131): `tryKitPathOf` is the `tryKitPathOf` of the folder it was built over. `copyInFile` joins the data folder's segments under the kit folder with the platform's separator and creates the folder when missing. The names of its files and folders are the taken paths. The bytes go to the chosen path through `writeNewBytesAtomically`, and the answer is built from those bytes by the decode and hash of `readDataFile` (step 128), one body for both. Every IO exception and `FileIoExn` is `KitIoErr` naming the file, as in step 126. (5) `KitProxy.readOnlyView` (step 131) refuses `copyInFile` with `KitReadOnlyErr` naming it, writing nothing, and passes `tryKitPathOf` through. No retry, overwrite option, cache or other field is added. Tests, in `KitProxyTests.fs`. `KitTestFolder` (step 125) gains three fields, each with a one-line doc. `absoluteName : string -> FileName` is the absolute name of a kit-relative path in this folder: under `kitFolder` in memory, and `Path.Combine` of the folder and the path on disk. `outsideName : string -> FileName` is an absolute name outside the kit: under `C:/outside` in memory, and on disk under a sibling folder `outside-<GUID>` of the kit folder, never created. `removeLabFile : string -> unit` is an outside writer deleting a file. New `KitProxyContract` facts, so `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests` both run them, each over an initialised folder (step 125): `a copied-in file keeps its name and bytes, and a taken name gets the next free suffix`: `copyInFile KitDataFolder.root (FileName "run 1.csv")` of the UTF-8 bytes of `phi,I\n0,0.5\n` answers `data/run 1.csv` with that text and the hash of those bytes, and `readDataFile` of it answers the same. A second copy of other bytes under the same leaf answers `data/run 1 (2).csv`, and a third `data/run 1 (3).csv`, while `data/run 1.csv` keeps its text. `paths` holds the three and no `*.tmp`. `copying into a new folder inside data creates it`: a copy into `KitDataFolder.tryCreate` of `data/raw/2026-11-03` creates that folder and its parent, and `paths` lists `data/raw`, `data/raw/2026-11-03` and the file. `a file inside the kit is located by its absolute name, and one outside it is not`: `tryKitPathOf (absoluteName "data/run 1.csv")` answers `data/run 1.csv` whether or not the file exists, and `tryKitPathOf (outsideName "run 1.csv")` answers `None`. `a read-only kit refuses a copy-in and writes nothing`: through `readOnlyView`, `copyInFile` answers `KitReadOnlyErr` and `paths` is unchanged. `KitProxyFolderTests` gains `a copied-in file holds exactly the bytes given, a byte-order mark included`: copied-in bytes EF BB BF followed by the UTF-8 of `a,b\n` are the file's bytes exactly, and the answer's text is `a,b\n` with the hash of all the bytes; and `the new-file writer refuses a file that exists, keeps it whole and leaves no temporary file`: over a file `x.csv` the test wrote, `writeNewBytesAtomically` of other bytes answers `FileIoExn`, the file keeps its bytes, and the folder holds no `*.tmp`.

**Acceptance.** After copy-in lands, both `KitProxy` implementations MUST copy a lab file's bytes into the kit's data folder under its own name or the next free suffix, never replacing a file, and MUST locate names inside the kit; constructor-unit-tests MUST pass, including `a copied-in file keeps its name and bytes, and a taken name gets the next free suffix`, `copying into a new folder inside data creates it`, `a file inside the kit is located by its absolute name, and one outside it is not`, `a read-only kit refuses a copy-in and writes nothing` under `KitProxyTests` and `KitProxyFolderTests`, `a copied-in file holds exactly the bytes given, a byte-order mark included` and `the new-file writer refuses a file that exists, keeps it whole and leaves no temporary file`, the count rising by 10, with every step 126 and step 127 fact passing as written; and build, elevation and the eleven s16 invariants MUST pass.
